@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-validate-applypatch-inputs-as-json-values
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate applyPatch inputs as JSON values"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` receives JavaScript values, but RFC 6902 operates on JSON documents. The previous
+validation allowed JavaScript values such as `Date`, sparse arrays, and non-finite numbers, which
+could be silently changed during cloning instead of producing a patch error.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate the document, patch document, and operation values as JSON-shaped JavaScript data before
+applying a patch. Accept finite JSON primitives, dense arrays, and own data properties on ordinary
+or null-prototype objects; reject other JavaScript-specific representations.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Invalid input fails before operation evaluation, so JSON Patch behavior is not altered by JavaScript
+serialization or cloning quirks. RFC-defined sequential operation evaluation and first-error
+termination remain unchanged.
